   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "story": "Bev and Gus Lindgren hosted Tamsin River Campground every summer for nine years. When the Cordon shut Route 9 there were still eleven campers on the loop, and Bev kept order: fees in the lockbox, quiet hours at ten, water from the spigot boiled, flour and salt left for the painted people on the rise. In September the fever started at the Haldanes' motorhome. Bev turned the shower house into a sick ward and chained the men's side when the Haldane boys started biting. Gus took sick last; she rigged her door alarm on the bedroom so she would hear him get up, padlocked the trailer behind her and went back to nurse the others, her keys on the utility-room hook. The register in the fee station says who left and who stayed.",
